# Vendored data notice

`data/pc/1.8/` contains a small, pinned subset of
[PrismarineJS/minecraft-data](https://github.com/PrismarineJS/minecraft-data), fetched from `master`
on 2026-11-20. `minecraft-data` is distributed under the MIT license (see its `package.json` and the
upstream repository); this notice is kept so the provenance is never lost.

Only the files needed for the M1 data loader and codec compiler are included. The upstream
`version.json` reports `minecraftVersion: 1.8.8` and `version: 47`; Minecraft 1.8.9 uses the same
protocol and data, so docs refer to the reference target as **1.8.9 / protocol 47**.

To support another version, add its `pc/<version>` files and an entry in `data/dataPaths.json`, or
point `PYFLAYER_DATA_DIR` at a full `minecraft-data/data` checkout.
